The proof rewrites the term $-\sum_{f\in\mathcal{F}_h}\int_f\llbracket\vb_hrbracket\cdot\{\mu^{-1}
abla	imes\Eb\}$ via \eqref{eqn1.11} into an element-boundary integral plus the interior-face term $-\sum_{f\in\mathcal{F}_h^{\mathcal{I}}}\int_f\llbracket\mu^{-1}
abla	imes\Ebrbracket\cdot\{\vb_h\}\,\mathrm{d}S$, and then discards that term invoking only $\llbracket
abla	imes\Ebrbracket=\zerob$. Since $\mu$ is only piecewise smooth and may jump across material interfaces, $\llbracket\mu^{-1}
abla	imes\Ebrbracket$ need not vanish, so the inference is invalid as written; the discarded term vanishes only via the Maxwell interface condition (tangential continuity of $\mu^{-1}
abla	imes\Eb$ for the exact solution), which the source never invokes. The same unargued discard of the $-\sum_{f\in\mathcal{F}_h^{\mathcal{I}}}\int_f\llbracket\mu^{-1}
abla	imes\Ebrbracket\cdot\{\Eb_I-\Eb_h\}$ term occurs in the proof of Theorem ef{theorem4.2}.
